  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TRAIDE Ethiopia 2.0</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The TRAIDE Ethiopia Phase II program builds on Phase I to advance sustainable and inclusive economic development in Ethiopia through private-sector development led by the TRAIDE Foundation.
It focuses on identifying, designing, and scaling Dutch-Ethiopian business partnerships, while also involving companies from other countries where relevant.

The program applies a refined TRAIDE Methodology that moves from assessing local challenges and opportunities to developing concepts, building partnerships, mobilising external finance for partnerships, and scaling impact.
Core activities include market assessments aligned with the NL priorities in Ethiopia and facilitation of partnerships across business, government, research, and civil society.

Priority sectors include agriculture, health, and water management, each addressing concrete challenges such as farmer productivity, healthcare access, and water loss.

Responsible Business Conduct within the new business partnerships is strengthened through thematic learning sessions, stakeholder dialogues, and sector roundtables.</narrative>
  </description>
